@@ -9,5 +9,4 @@
 title: Jacobian-coupled block-term model with a structure-revealing DP floor
 eli5: "Tried to make a block-term model's differential-privacy floor depend on the inter-block spectral gap, a structure-revealing privacy advantage the parent COVERT model could not give. The mechanism: release whitened block scores (S = T G^{-1/2}) so the coupling Jacobian stops being block-diagonal and the gap enters the floor."
 outcome: "NO-GO. The matched-rho test showed the whitening advantage is generic R-block-Gram preconditioning, shared by flat/P3LS linear models: block-term L=2 tracks FLAT, with no multilinearity scaling (same trap as COVERT). The within-block multiway structure never enters the coupling. Don't re-attempt without a genuinely different mechanism"
